meta:
  origin:
    # Data product / Snapshot
    title: "Childhood in Nineteenth-Century France"
    description: |-
      A study of childhood among the peasantry and the working classes of nineteenth-century France, covering children's work in the countryside and in industry, their health, their schooling, and the child labor legislation of 1841 and 1874.

      The figure taken from this book here is the share of children aged 10-14 recorded as working in France in 1896.
    date_published: "1988"

    # Citation
    producer: Heywood
    citation_full: |-
      Heywood, C. (1988). Childhood in Nineteenth-Century France: Work, Health and Education among the 'Classes Populaires'. Cambridge University Press.

